{#-
GPT-2 chat template (concatenation shim)
GPT-2 predates chat models — there is NO authentic chat format.
This template makes /v1/chat/completions degrade gracefully to what
GPT-2 actually is: a text completion engine. All message contents
(system, user, assistant) are concatenated verbatim with NO separators
and NO special tokens (ChatML <|im_end|> etc. are not in the GPT-2
vocab — the default fallback would tokenize them as garbage text).

Single-turn = identical to raw /v1/completions. Multi-turn concatenates
turns as one document, the best a base model can do.

The authentic interface remains /v1/completions. This shim only exists
so chat-endpoint callers get clean continuation instead of ChatML noise.
-#}
{%- for message in messages -%}
{{- message.content -}}
{%- endfor -%}